{"id":"e3b01159c2b5601b","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-thm-fodor.md","title":"Fodor's Lemma","display":"thm-fodor — Fodor's Lemma","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-fodor","aliases":["58-thm-fodor","Fodor's Lemma","Pressing-Down Lemma"],"display":"thm-fodor — Fodor's Lemma","depends_on":["[[58-df-stationary]]","[[58-df-regressive-function]]","[[58-df-regular]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-fodor"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-fodor</span><span>Fodor's Lemma</span><span>Pressing-Down Lemma</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-fodor — Fodor's Lemma"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"b802c3dd76418d95\" href=\"?note=b802c3dd76418d95\" title=\"58-df-stationary\">58-df-stationary</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"aa5065a1f0bd9a7f\" href=\"?note=aa5065a1f0bd9a7f\" title=\"58-df-regressive-function\">58-df-regressive-function</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d83de8696e4dad26\" href=\"?note=d83de8696e4dad26\" title=\"58-df-regular\">58-df-regular</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa,S,f\\in V\">\\(\\kappa,S,f\\in V\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Reg}(\\kappa)\">\\(\\mathrm{Reg}(\\kappa)\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\">\\(\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\">\\(\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\\)</span> are the exact source predicates.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}fodor}\\vdash \\omega&lt;\\kappa\\land\\mathrm{Reg}(\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\\to\\exists\\gamma&lt;\\kappa\\;\\mathrm{Stationary}(\\{\\alpha\\in S:f(\\alpha)=\\gamma\\},\\kappa).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}fodor}\\vdash \\omega&lt;\\kappa\\land\\mathrm{Reg}(\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Stationary}(S,\\kappa)\\land\\mathrm{Regressive}_S(f,S)\\to\\exists\\gamma&lt;\\kappa\\;\\mathrm{Stationary}(\\{\\alpha\\in S:f(\\alpha)=\\gamma\\},\\kappa).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Equivalently, a regressive function on a stationary set is constant on a stationary subset.</li>\n<li>Since stationary subsets of regular uncountable <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> have cardinality <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>, the fiber above <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\gamma\">\\(\\gamma\\)</span> has size <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-stationary","status":"resolved","id":"b802c3dd76418d95","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-stationary]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-regressive-function","status":"resolved","id":"aa5065a1f0bd9a7f","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-regressive-function]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-regular","status":"resolved","id":"d83de8696e4dad26","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-regular]]",